## showViewer

this project is an idea on how to generate custom vj loops based on an audio file and the frequecies produced from it.

The scene picker includes a procedural Reactive shader loop with audio-reactive petals and rings: beat onsets pulse the bloom, mids smoothly transition between petal counts, and treble adds ring glints. Choose a palette preset or adjust the primary and secondary colors.

The Reactive scene can export a silent, seamless 16-second MP4 at 30 fps in HD (1280x720) or Full HD (1920x1080). Export uses the analyzed audio spectrum when available and requires `ffmpeg` with the `libx264` encoder installed on `PATH`. The renderer requires an OpenGL 3.3-compatible renderer.

## why build this
as someone who makes visuals for shows, i was curious to see if i could generate vj loops, and so this is the prototype

## to use

in order to use this, you can just install it via cargo using:

```
cargo install showViewer
```